{
  "title": "19: Maryam مريم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nكٓهٰيٰعٓصٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nKAAHAAYAAA’AASAA.\nKaf. Ha. Ya. Ain. Sad. (K. H. Y. A. S.)\nذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهٗ زَكَرِيَّا ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(2)\nZEKRU RAHMATE RABBEKA A’ABDAH ZAKAREEA.\n(This is) a mention of the mercy of thy Lord unto His servant Zachariah.\nاِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗ نِدَآءً خَفِيًّا‏(3)\nIZ NAADAA WAL NEDAAAN KHAFEEA.\nWhen called he unto his Lord (with) prayer in low voice.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّىْ وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّاْسُ شَيْبًا وَّلَمْ اَكُنْۢ بِدُعَآئِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا‏(4)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE WAHANA AL-A’AZMU MINNEE WAASHTAA’ALA AR-RAASU SHAYBAN LAM AAKUN BEDUA’AAEKA RABBE SHAQEEA.\nSaid he: “O’ my Lord! Verily my bones are weakened and my head doth glisten with grey hoariness: but never am I in my prayer unto Thee, O’ my Lord! been unblest!\nوَاِنِّىْ خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِىَ مِنْ وَّرَآءِىْ وَكَانَتِ امْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ لِىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا ۙ‏(5)\nWA INNEE KHEFTU AL-MAWAALEAAA MIN WWARAAEAA KAANATIL AMRAATEAA A’AAQERAN FAHAB LEE MIN LLADUNKA WALIYYANW.\nAnd verily I fear my kindred (cousins) after me, and my wife is barren, So grant me from Thyself an heir!\nيَّرِثُنِىْ وَيَرِثُ مِنْ اٰلِ يَعْقُوْبَ ۖ  وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا‏(6)\nYYARESUNEAA WAYARESU MIN AALE YA’QOOBAL WAAJA’ALHU RABBE RAZEEA.\nWho shall inherit me and inherit from the family of Jacob; and make him O’ my Lord! one with whom Thou art well pleased!\nيٰزَكَرِيَّاۤ اِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلٰم اۨسْمُهٗ يَحْيٰى ۙ لَمْ نَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا‏(7)\nYAAZAKAREEA INNAA NUBASSHERUKA BEGHULAAM FEEHAS YAHYAA LAM NAJ-A’L LAHU MIN QABLO SAMEEA.\n(The Lord responded to the prayer saying): “O’ Zachariah! Verily We give thee the glad tidings of a son, his name shall be Yahya (John), and We gave not to any one before (him) that name!\nقَالَ رَبِّ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّكَانَتِ امْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرًا وَّقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا‏(8)\nQAALA RABBE ANNAA LAHUL LEE GHULAAMUN WWAKAANATE AMRAATEAA A’AAQERAN WWAQAD BALAGHTU MENAL AL-KEBARE E’ETEEA.\nSaid he: “O’ my Lord! How can there be for me a son while my wife is barren and indeed I have reached of the old age the extreme infirmity?\nقَالَ كَذٰلِكَ‌ۚ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ وَّقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا‏(9)\nQAALA KAZAALEKA QAALA RABBOKA HOWA A’LAYYA HAYNUN WWAQAD KHALAQTUKA MIN QABLO WA LAM TAKU SHAY-ANW.\nSaid He (the Lord): “So shall it be.” Thy Lord sayeth: “Easy is it to Me, for indeed have I created thee aforetime, when thou wert nothing!\nقَالَ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِّىْۤ اٰيَةً‌  ؕ قَالَ اٰيَتُكَ اَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلٰثَ لَيَالٍ سَوِيًّا‏(10)\nQAALA RABBE A’L LEE AAYATAL QAALA AAAYATUKA ALLAA TUKALLEMA NAASA SALAASA LAYAALIN SAWIYYAN.\nSaid he: “O’ my Lord! Vouchsafe me a sign!” He said: “Thy sign is that thou speaketh not to the people for three nights, though sound (in health)!\nفَخَرَجَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖ مِنَ الْمِحْرَابِ فَاَوْحٰٓى اِلَيْهِمْ اَنْ سَبِّحُوْا بُكْرَةً وَّعَشِيًّا‏(11)\nFAKHARAJA A’LAA QAWMEHI MENAL AL-MEHRAABE FAAWHAAA ELAYHIM AN SABBEHOOA BUKRATANW WWAA’ASHEEA.\nThen he went out (of the sanctuary) unto his people and made signs unto them (with his hands) that they should glorify (God) morning and evening.\nيٰيَحْيٰى خُذِ الْكِتٰبَ بِقُوَّةٍ‌ ؕ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا ۙ‏(12)\nYAAYAHYAA KHUZE KETAABA BE-QUWWATINW WA AATAYNAAHO AL-HUKMA SABEEA.\n(The Lord said unto Zachariah’s son) “O’ Yahya! Hold thou the Book fast!” and We granted him wisdom (apostleship) while yet a child.\nوَّحَنَانًا مِّنْ لَّدُنَّا وَزَكٰوةً  ‌ؕ وَّكَانَ تَقِيًّا ۙ‏(13)\nWWAHANAANAN MIN WA WAZAKAAWTAN WA KAANA TAQEEA.\nAnd compassion as from Us and purity, and pious one was he,\nوَّبَرًّۢا بِوَالِدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ جَبَّارًا عَصِيًّا‏(14)\nWWABARRAN INSAANA WA LAM YAKUL JABBAARAN A’ASEEA.\nAnd duteous unto his parents, and neither insolent (nor) disobedient.\nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوْتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّا‏(15)\nWA SALAAMUN A’LAYHE YAWMA WULEDA WA YAWMA YAMOOTO WA YAWMA YUBA’ASU HAYYANW.\nPeace be on him the day he was born, and the day he dieth, and the day he is raised (once again) to life.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مَرْيَمَ‌ۘ اِذِ انْتَبَذَتْ مِنْ اَهْلِهَا مَكَانًا شَرْقِيًّا ۙ‏(16)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE MARYAMAL EZIM ANTABAZAT MIN AHLEHAA MAKAANAN SHARQEEA.\nAnd mention in the Book (Qur’an) about Mary (also) when she withdrew herself from her family (in the house) eastward\nفَاتَّخَذَتْ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْ حِجَابًا فَاَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهَا رُوْحَنَا فَتَمَثَّلَ لَهَا بَشَرًا سَوِيًّا‏(17)\nFAATTAKHAZAT MIN DOONEHEM HEJAABAN FA-ARSALNAA ELAYHAA ROOHANAA FATAMASSALA LAHAA BASHARAN SAWIYYAN.\nThen she took a veil (cover herself) from them; then sent We unto her Our Spirit, then he (the Spirit) appeared to her a man sound (in form)\nقَالَتْ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِالرَّحْمٰنِ مِنْكَ اِنْ كُنْتَ تَقِيًّا‏(18)\nQAALAT INNEE A-OO’ZO BE-RAHMAANIR MENKA IN KUNTA TAQEEA.\nSaid she: “Verily I fly for refuge in The Beneficent (God) from thee, (be gone from me) if thou art God-fearing\n‌قَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا رَسُوْلُ رَبِّكِ ‌ ۖ  لِاَهَبَ لَكِ غُلٰمًا زَكِيًّا‏(19)\nQAALA INNAMAA ANAA RASOOLAL RABBEKE LEAAHABA LAKE GHULAAMAN ZAKEEA.\nSaid he: “I am only a messenger (Angel) of thy Lord: so that I give to thee a son purified.\nقَالَتْ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِىْ بَشَرٌ وَّلَمْ اَكُ بَغِيًّا‏(20)\nQAALAT ANNAA LAHUL LEE GHULAAMUN LAM YAMSASNEAA BASHARUM LAM AAKU BAGHEEA.\nSaid she: “How can there be unto me a son while hath not touched me (any) man and nor was I unchaste!\nقَالَ كَذٰلِكِ‌ ۚ قَالَ رَبُّكِ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ‌ ۚ وَلِنَجْعَلَهٗۤ اٰيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِّنَّا‌ ۚ وَكَانَ اَمْرًا مَّقْضِيًّا‏(21)\nQAALA KAZAALEKE QAALA RABBUKE HOWA A’LAYYA HAYNUN WALENAJA’ALAH AAYATAL LIN-NAASE WA RAHMATAM MINNAA KAANAL AMRAN MMAQZEEA.\nSaid he “So shall it be; thy Lord sayeth, It is easy for Me, and that We will make him a Sign (miracle) (of Ours) unto the people and a Mercy from Us; It is a matter (already) decreed.\nفَحَمَلَتْهُ فَانْتَبَذَتْ بِهٖ مَكَانًا قَصِيًّا‏(22)\nFA-HAMALATHO FANTABAZAT BEHI MAKAANAN QASIYYAA.\nSo she conceived him and retired with him (away from her people) to a remote place.\nفَاَجَآءَهَا الْمَخَاضُ اِلٰى جِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ‌ۚ قَالَتْ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ مِتُّ قَبْلَ هٰذَا وَكُنْتُ نَسْيًا مَّنْسِيًّا‏(23)\nFA-AJAAA-AHAL MAKHAAZO ELAA JIZ-I’N NAKHLAH, QAALAT YAA LAYTANEE MITTO QABLA HAAZAA WA KUNTO NASYAM MANSIYYAA.\nAnd the throes (of childbirth) forced her to betake herself unto the trunk of a palm-tree. She said: “Oh! Had I died ere this, and had been lost in oblivion totally forgotten!\nفَنَادٰٮهَا مِنْ تَحْتِهَاۤ اَلَّا تَحْزَنِىْ قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا‏(24)\nFA-NAADAAHAA MIN TAHTEHAA ALLAA TAHZANEE QAD JA-A’LA RABBOKE TAHTAKE SARIYYAA.\nThen (a voice) called out unto her from beneath her; “Grieve not thou, verily thy Lord hath caused from beneath thee, (to flow) a stream!\nوَهُزِّىْۤ اِلَيْكِ بِجِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ تُسٰقِطْ عَلَيْكِ رُطَبًا جَنِيًّا‏(25)\nWA HUZZEE ELAYKE BE-JIZ-I’N NAKHLATE TOSAAQIT A’LAYKE ROTABAN JANIYYAA.\nAnd shake towards thee the trunk of the palm-tree, it will drop on thee dates fresh (and) ripe.\nفَكُلِىْ وَاشْرَبِىْ وَقَرِّىْ عَيْنًا‌ ۚ فَاِمَّا تَرَيِنَّ مِنَ الْبَشَرِ اَحَدًا ۙ فَقُوْلِىْۤ اِنِّىْ نَذَرْتُ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ صَوْمًا فَلَنْ اُكَلِّمَ الْيَوْمَ اِنْسِيًّا ‌ۚ‏(26)\nFA-KOLEE WASHRABEE WA QARREE A’YNAA, FA-IMMAA TARAYINNA MENAL BASHARE AHADAN, FA-QOOLEE INNEE NAZARTO LIR-RAHMAANE SAWMAA FA-LAN OKALLEMAL YAWMA INSIYYAA.\nThen eat and drink and refresh the eye. Then if thou seest any man say: “Verily I have vowed unto the Beneficent (God) a fast so never shall I speak today unto any man.\nفَاَتَتْ بِهٖ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهٗ‌ؕ قَالُوْا يٰمَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا‏(27)\nFA-ATAT BEHI QAWMAHAA TAHMELOH, QAALOO YAA MARYAMO LAQAD JEATE SHAY-AN FARIYYAA.\nAnd she came with him unto her people carrying him (with her). Said they: “O’ Mary! Indeed thou hath come with an unusual thing!\nيٰۤاُخْتَ هٰرُوْنَ مَا كَانَ اَ بُوْكِ امْرَاَ سَوْءٍ وَّمَا كَانَتْ اُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(28)\nYAA UKHTA HAAROONA MAA KAANA ABOOKIM RA-A SAWINW WA MAA KAANAT UMMOKE BAGHIYYAA.\nO’ sister of Aaron! thy father was not a bad man, nor was thy mother an unchaste woman!\nفَاَشَارَتْ اِلَيْهِ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا كَيْفَ نُكَلِّمُ مَنْ كَانَ فِى الْمَهْدِ صَبِيًّا‏(29)\nFA-ASHAARAT ELAYH, QAALOO KAYFA NOKALLEMO MAN KAANA FIL MAHDE SABIYYAA.\nBut she pointed unto him. They said: “How can we speak unto one who is (yet) a child in the cradle\nقَالَ اِنِّىْ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اٰتٰٮنِىَ الْكِتٰبَ وَجَعَلَنِىْ نَبِيًّا ۙ‏(30)\nQAALA INNEE A’BDUL LAAH, AATAANEYAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LANEE NABIYYANW.\nHe (Jesus miraculously) said: “Verily I am a servant of God; He hath given me a Book (Evangel) and made me a Prophet!\nوَّجَعَلَنِىْ مُبٰرَكًا اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُ وَاَوْصٰنِىْ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَالزَّكٰوةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا ‌ۖ ‏(31)\nWA JA-A’LANEE MOBAARAKAN AYNA MAA KUNT, WA AWSAANEE BIS-SALAATE WAZ ZAKAATE MAA DUMTO HAYYANW.\nAnd He hath made me blessed wherever I be and He hath enjoined on me prayer and poor-rate so long as I live!\nوَّبَرًّۢابِوَالِدَتِىْ وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِىْ جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا‏(32)\nWA BARRAM BE-WAALEDATEE, WA LAM YAJ-A’LNEE JABBAARAN SHAQIYYAA.\nAnd (to be) duteous to my mother, and He hath not made me insolent unblest!\nوَالسَّلٰمُ عَلَىَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدْتُّ وَيَوْمَ اَمُوْتُ وَيَوْمَ اُبْعَثُ حَيًّا‏(33)\nWAS SALAAMO A’LAYYA YAWMA WOLIDTO WA YAWMA AMOOTO WA YAWMA UB-A’SO HAYYAA.\nAnd peace be on me day I was born, and the day I die, and the day I am raised alive ”!\nذٰ لِكَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ‌ۚ قَوْلَ الْحَقِّ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ يَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(34)\nZAALEKA E’ESAB NO MARYAM, QAWLAL HAQQIL LAZEE FEEHE YAMTAROON.\nThis is Jesus, the son of Mary; (this is) a statement of the truth about which they dispute.\nمَا كَانَ لِلّٰهِ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ مِنْ وَّلَدٍ‌ۙ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ؕ اِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُؕ‏(35)\nMAA KAANA LILLAAHE ANY YATTAKHEZA MINW WALADIN, SUBHAANAH, EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FA-YAKOON.\nIt beseemeth not God that He should take unto Himself a son, glory be to Him; when a matter is decreed, He only sayeth unto it ‘Be’ and it is\nوَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ ‌ؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(36)\nWA INNAL LAAHA RABBEE WA RABBOKUM FA’BODOOH, HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd verily God is my Lord and your Lord, so worship (only) Him; this is the right way.\nفَاخْتَلَفَ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِهِمْ‌ۚ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ مَّشْهَدِ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(37)\nFAKHTALAFAL AHZAABO MIM BAYNEHIM, FA-WAYLUL LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO MIM MASH-HADE YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nThen did differ the sects among themselves and woe unto those who disbelieved, because of their presenting themselves on the great day.\nاَسْمِعْ بِهِمْ وَاَبْصِرْۙ يَوْمَ يَاْتُوْنَنَا‌ لٰكِنِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ الْيَوْمَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\nAASMEA’ BEHIM WAABSER YAWMA YAATOONANAA LAAKENE ZAALEMOON YAWMA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nHow clearly shall they hear and how clearly shall they see on the day when they appear unto Us, but the unjust this day are in manifest straying.\nوَاَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ اِذْ قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ‌‌ۘ وَهُمْ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(39)\nWAANZERHUM YAWMA AL-HASRATE IZ QUZEAAA MIN WA HUM FEE GHAFLATIM WA HUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nAnd warn them of the intense regret, when the matter shall have been decreed while they are (now) in negligence and they believe not.\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نَرِثُ الْاَرْضَ وَمَنْ عَلَيْهَا وَاِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(40)\nINNAA NAHNO NARESU ARZA WA MAN A’LAYHAA WA ELAYNAA YARJEO’ON.\nVerily We inherit the earth and those who are on it, and unto Us shall they be returned.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ ۙ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صِدِّيْقًا نَّبِيًّا‏(41)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE IBRAAHEEMA INNAHU KAANA SEDDEEQAN NNABEEA.\nAnd (make) mention in the Book (Qur’an) Abraham; verily he was a man of Truth, an Apostle (of Ours).\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ يٰۤاَبَتِ لِمَ تَعْبُدُ مَا لَا يَسْمَعُ وَلَا يُبْصِرُ وَ لَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْكَ شَيْئًا‏(42)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE YAA LEMA TAA’BUDU MAA LAA YASMA-O’ WA LAA YUBSERU WA LAA YUGHNEE A’NKAL SHAY-ANW.\nWhen said he unto his father, “O’ My Father! Why worshippeth thou that which heareth not, nor doth it see, nor doth it avail thee in aught?\nيٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْ قَدْ جَآءَنِىْ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ مَا لَمْ يَاْتِكَ فَاتَّبِعْنِىْۤ اَهْدِكَ صِرَاطًا سَوِيًّا‏(43)\nYAA INNEE QAD JAAANEAA MENAL I’LME MAA LAM YAATEKA FAATTABEA’NEAA AAHDEKA SERAATAM SAWIYYAN.\nO’ my father! Indeed hath come unto me, of the knowledge which hath not come unto thee, so follow me: I will guide thee on the path (which is) straight.\nيٰۤاَبَتِ لَا تَعْبُدِ الشَّيْطٰنَ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ عَصِيًّا‏(44)\nYAA LAA TAA’BUDE ASH-SHAYTAANA INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA KAANA LELRRAHMAANE A’ASEEA.\nO’ my father! Worship not Satan; Verily Satan unto the Beneficent (God), was disobedient”.\nيٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يَّمَسَّكَ عَذَابٌ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ فَتَكُوْنَ لِلشَّيْطٰنِ وَلِيًّا‏(45)\nYAA INNEE AKHAAFO AN YYAMASSAKA A’ZAABUN MENAL RAHMAANIR FA TAKOONA LELSSHAYTAANE WALIYYANW.\nO’ my father! Verily I fear that toucheth thee chastisement from the Beneficent (God), so that thou be unto Satan a friend.\nقَالَ اَرَاغِبٌ اَنْتَ عَنْ اٰلِهَتِىْ يٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُ‌ۚ لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ لَاَرْجُمَنَّكَ‌ وَاهْجُرْنِىْ مَلِيًّا‏(46)\nQAALA AARAAGHEBUN ANTA A’N AAALEHATEAA YAABRAAHEEMU LAIL LAM TANTAHE LAARJUMANNAKA WAAHJURNEAA MALEEA.\nSaid he: “Inclineth thou against my gods, O’ Abraham; If thou didst desist not certainly I will stone thee; Begone from me for a long while.\nقَالَ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكَ‌ۚ سَاَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّىْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِىْ حَفِيًّا‏(47)\nQAALA SALAAMUN A’LAYKA SAASTAGHFERU LAKA RABBEAA INNAHU KAANA BEE HAFEEA.\nSaid he: “Peace be on thee, I will pray unto my Lord to forgive thee; Verily He unto me is most gracious.\nوَ اَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَاَدْعُوْا رَبِّىْ‌ ‌ۖ  عَسٰٓى اَلَّاۤ اَكُوْنَ بِدُعَآءِ رَبِّىْ شَقِيًّا‏(48)\nWA AAA’TAZELUKUM WA MAA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAADU’OOA RABBEE A’SAA ALLAA SHAY-IWN WA BE-DO-A’AA-IL RABBEE SHAQEEA.\nI withdraw from you (all) and what ye call upon other than God, and I call upon (only) my Lord; Happly in my prayer unto my Lord I shall not be unblest.\nفَلَمَّا اعْتَزَلَهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ۙ وَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ‌ ؕ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا نَبِيًّا‏(49)\nFALAMMAA AA’TAZALAHUM WA MAA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WAKULLAN JA-A’LNAA NABEEA.\nAnd when he withdrew from them and what they worshipped besides God, We granted unto him Isaac and Jacob; and each one of them made We an apostle.\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّحْمَتِنَا وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ عَلِيًّا‏(50)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHUM MIN RRAHMATENAA WA JA-A’LNAA LAHUM LESAANA SEDQIN A’ALEEA.\nAnd granted We unto them of Our mercy, and assigned unto them a lofty tongue of truth fulness.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مُوْسٰٓى‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مُخْلَصًا وَّكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَّبِيًّا‏(51)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE MOOSAA INNAHU KAANA MUKHLASAN WA KAANA RASOOLAM NNABEEA.\nAnd mention in the Book (Qur’an) about Moses; Verily he was one freed, and he was an Apostle and a Prophet.\nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ الْاَيْمَنِ وَقَرَّبْنٰهُ نَجِيًّا‏(52)\nWANAADAYNAAHU MIN JAANEBIT TOORE AYMANE WAQARRABNAAHU NAJEEA.\nAnd We called unto him from the right side of the Mount Sinai, and made him draw nigh (unto Us) for a communion.\nوَ وَهَبْنَا لَهٗ مِنْ رَّحْمَتِنَاۤ اَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ نَبِيًّا‏(53)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU MIN RRAHMATENAA AAKHAAHU AALO NABEEA.\nAnd granted We unto him out of Our mercy his brother Aaron, (also) a Prophet.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صَادِقَ الْوَعْدِ وَكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَّبِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(54)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE AESMAAE’EELA INNAHU KAANA SAADEQA AL-WAA’DE KAANAL RASOOLAM NNABEEA.\nAnd (make) mention in the Book (Qur’an) Ishmael verily he was (ever) true to his promise, and he was an Apostle, a Prophet.\nوَ كَانَ يَاْمُرُ اَهْلَهٗ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَالزَّكٰوةِ وَكَانَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ مَرْضِيًّا‏(55)\nWA KAANA YAAMURU AHLAHU BEALSSALAAWTE WAALZZAKAAWTE KAANAL I’NDAL RABBEHI MARZEEA.\nAnd he was enjoining on his family, prayer and charity and was he unto his Lord well-pleasing.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِدْرِيْسَ‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صِدِّيْقًا نَّبِيًّا ۙ ‏(56)\nWAAZKUR FIL KETAABE AEDREESA INNAHU KAANA SEDDEEQAN NNABEEA.\nAnd mention in the Book (Qur’an) (about) Idris; verily he was a truthful one, a Prophet.\nوَّرَفَعْنٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا‏(57)\nWWARAFAA’NAAHU MAKAANAN A’ALEEA.\nAnd We exalted him to a high station.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ اٰدَمَ وَمِمَّنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوْحٍ وَّمِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَمِمَّنْ هَدَيْنَا وَاجْتَبَيْنَا‌ ؕ اِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُ الرَّحْمٰنِ خَرُّوْا سُجَّدًا وَّبُكِيًّا ۩‏(58)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM MENAL NABIYYEENA MIN ZURREETE AADAMAL WA MIMMAN HAMALNAA LAAHA NOOHIN WA MIN ZURREETE IBRAAHEEMA WA ISRAAA-EELAZ WA MIMMAN HADAYNAA WAAJTABAYNAA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATUL RAHMAANIR KHARROOA SUJJADANW WWABUKEEA.\nThese are they on whom did God bestow (His) bounties, from among the prophets of the posterity of Adam; and of those whom We did bare with Noah, and of the posterity of Abraham and Israel, and of those whom We did guide and We did choose; When the signs of the Beneficent (God) were rehearsed unto them, they fell down prostrating (in obeisance) and weeping.\nفَخَلَفَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ اَضَاعُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاتَّبَعُوا الشَّهَوٰتِ‌ فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا ۙ‏(59)\nFAKHALAFA MIN BA’DEHIM KHALFUN AAZAAU’OOA SALAATA WAATTABAU’OOA ASH-SHAHAWTE FA-SAWFA YALQAWNA GHAYA.\nBut followed after them a succession who neglected prayers and they followed lust, so they shall soon meet perdition,\nاِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا ۙ‏(60)\nILLAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON SHAY-ANW.\nExcept he who repented and believed and did good, then these shall enter the garden {of Paradise), and they shall not be dealt with unjustly in aught,\nجَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ اۨلَّتِىْ وَعَدَ الرَّحْمٰنُ عِبَادَهٗ بِالْغَيْبِ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ وَعْدُهٗ مَاْتِيًّا‏(61)\nJANNATIN A’ADNIN LATEE WA-A’DAR RAHMAANO E’EBAADAH BIL-GHAYBE INNAHU KAANA WA’DOHU MAATEEA.\nThe gardens of eternity which the Beneficent (God) hath promised unto His servants, while unseen; Verily His promise shall come to pass.\nلَّا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا اِلَّا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ وَلَهُمْ رِزْقُهُمْ فِيْهَا بُكْرَةً وَّعَشِيًّا‏(62)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA FEEHAA LAGHWANW ILLAA SALAAMAN WA LAHUM REZQUHUM FEEHAA BUKRATANW WWAA’ASHEEA.\nThey will hear not therein any vain discourse, but only ‘Peace’, and they shall have their sustenance therein, morning and evening.\nتِلْكَ الْجَنَّةُ الَّتِىْ نُوْرِثُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا مَنْ كَانَ تَقِيًّا‏(63)\nTILKA JANNATO LATEE NOORESU MIN E’EBAADENAA MAN KAANA TAQEEA.\nThis is the garden (Paradise) which We shall cause to be inherited by those of Our servants who are pious.\nوَمَا نَتَنَزَّلُ اِلَّا بِاَمْرِ رَبِّكَ‌ ۚ لَهٗ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْنَا وَمَا خَلْفَنَا وَمَا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ‌ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ نَسِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(64)\nWA MAA NATANAZZALU ILLAA BE-AMRE RABBEKA LAHU MAA BAYNA AYDEENAA WA MAA KHALFANAA WA MAA BAYNA ZAA LEKA WA MAA KAANA RABBOKA NASEEA.\n(Say the angels, “O’ Apostle of God, Muhammad!) “We come not down (from heaven) but by the command of thy Lord; His is whatever is before us and whatever is behind us and whatever is between these! And thy Lord is not forgetful.\nرَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فَاعْبُدْهُ وَاصْطَبِرْ لِعِبَادَتِهٖ‌ؕ هَلْ تَعْلَمُ لَهٗ سَمِيًّا‏(65)\nRRABBU SAMAAWAATE WA ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FAAA’BUDHU WAASTABER LEE’EBAADATEH HAL TAA’LAMU LAHU SAMEEA.\nThe Lord of the heavens and the earth and what (ever) is between them; so worship Him (alone), and be steadfast in His worship! Knowest thou of any other (worthy of being) named (with) of the same name? (as He)?\nوَيَقُوْلُ الْاِنْسَانُ ءَاِذَا مَا مِتُّ لَسَوْفَ اُخْرَجُ حَيًّا‏(66)\nWA YAQOOLO INSAANO A-EZAA MAA METTU LASAWFA AUKHRAJU HAYYANW.\nAnd sayeth man: “What! When I am dead shall I be brought forth alive?\nاَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا‏(67)\nAWA LAA YAZKURU INSAANO ANNAA KHALAQNAAHO MIN QABLO WA LAM YAKU SHAY-ANW.\nWhat! Beareth not man in mind that We created him before when he was naught.\nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَحْشُرَنَّهُمْ وَالشَّيٰطِيْنَ ثُمَّ لَنُحْضِرَنَّهُمْ حَوْلَ جَهَنَّمَ جِثِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(68)\nFAWARABBEKA LANAHSHURANNAHUM WA SHAYAATEENA SUMMA LANUHZERANNAHUM HAWLA JAHANNAMA JESEEA.\nSo by thy Lord! Most certainly will we gather them together and the Satan, then shall We certainly bring them forth round the Hell on their knees.\nثُمَّ لَنَنْزِعَنَّ مِنْ كُلِّ شِيْعَةٍ اَيُّهُمْ اَشَدُّ عَلَى الرَّحْمٰنِ عِتِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(69)\nSUMMA LANANZEA’ANNA MIN KULLE SHEEA’ATIN AAYHUM ASHADDO A’LAL RAHMAANIR E’ETEEA.\nThen shall We certainly pick out from every group of them those who against the Beneficent (God) were more intensely rebellious.\nثُمَّ لَنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ اَوْلٰى بِهَا صِلِيًّا‏(70)\nSUMMA LANAHNU A-A’LAMO BE-LAZEENA HUM AAWLAA BEHAA SELEEA.\nAnd certainly, We do know best those who deserve most to be burnt therein.\nوَاِنْ مِّنْکُمْ اِلَّا وَارِدُهَا ‌ؕ كَانَ عَلٰى رَبِّكَ حَتْمًا مَّقْضِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(71)\nWA MENM ILLAA WAAREDUHAA KAANA A’LAA RABBEKA HATMAN MMAQZEEA.\nAnd (there is) not one of you but shall go down unto it; This is of thy Lord a decided (unavoidable) decree\nثُمَّ نُنَجِّى الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا وَّنَذَرُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ فِيْهَا جِثِيًّا‏(72)\nSUMMA NUNAJJEAA LAZEENA TAQAW WWANAZARU ZAALEMEEN FEEHAA JESEEA.\nAnd then will We deliver those who guarded (themselves) against evil, and We will leave the unjust on their knees.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا ۙ اَىُّ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ خَيْرٌ مَّقَامًا وَّاَحْسَنُ نَدِيًّا‏(73)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LILLAZEENA AAMANOO AAA AL-FAREEQAYNE KHAYRUL MMAQAAMAN WWAAHSANU NADEEA.\nAnd when Our clear signs are rehearsed unto them, say those who disbelieve unto those who believe, which of the two parties is best in position? And which is the most goodly company?\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ اَحْسَنُ اَثَاثًا وَّرِءْيًا‏(74)\nWA AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HUM AHSANO AASAASAN WWAREYAN.\nAnd how many of the generations We did destroy before them, they were (even) better in riches and in splendour.\nقُلْ مَنْ كَانَ فِى الضَّلٰلَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ مَدًّا ۚ‌ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا رَاَوْا مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَ اِمَّا الْعَذَابَ وَاِمَّا السَّاعَةَ ؕ فَسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ هُوَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضْعَفُ جُنْدًا‏(75)\nQUL MAN KAANA FIL AZ-ZALAALATE FALYAMDUD LAHUL RAHMAANO MADDAN HATTAA EZAA RA-AW MAA YOOA’ADOONA IMMAA A’ZAABA WA AMMAA SAA-A’TA FA SA-YA’LAMOONA MAN HOWA HOWA MMAKAANAN WWAAZA’AFU JUNDAN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “As to those who are in error, the Beneficent (God) will certainly lengthen the span (of their) life; until behold they what they were promised, be it the chastisement (in this world) or the Hour (of Doom); Then shall they know who is worse placed and (who is the) weakest in forces!\nوَيَزِيْدُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اهْتَدَوْا هُدًى‌ؕ وَالْبٰقِيٰتُ الصّٰلِحٰتُ خَيْرٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابًا وَّخَيْرٌ مَّرَدًّا‏(76)\nWAYAZEEDU LAAHO LAZEENA TADAW HUDAN WAL BAAQEETU AS-SAALEHAATU KHAYRUL I’NDAL RABBEKA SAWAABAN WWAKHAYRUN MMARADDAN.\nAnd God increaseth in guidance those who are guided aright; and the everlasting good deeds are best with thy Lord, in recompense and best in (the ultimate) return.\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ كَفَرَ بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَقَالَ لَاُوْتَيَنَّ مَالًا وَّوَلَدًا ؕ‏(77)\nAAFARAAYTA LAZEE KAFARA BE-AAYAATENAA WA QAALA LAAWTAYANNA MAALAWN WWAWALADAN.\nHave thou then seen him who disbelieveth in Our signs and sayeth: “I shall surely be given wealth and children (sons)\nاَطَّلَعَ الْغَيْبَ اَمِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمٰنِ عَهْدًا ۙ‏(78)\nAATTALAA’A GHAYBA AMIL TAKHAZA I’NDAL RAHMAANIR A’HDAN.\nHath he got into the (secret) knowledge of the unseen? or hath taken from the Beneficent (God) a promise?\nكَلَّا ‌ ؕ سَنَكْتُبُ مَا يَقُوْلُ وَنَمُدُّ لَهٗ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ مَدًّا ۙ‏(79)\nKALLAA SANAKTUBU MAA YAQOOLO WANAMUDDU LAHU MENAL A’ZAABE MADDAN.\nBy no means! We will write down what he sayeth and We will lengthen for him the length of the chastisement.\nوَّنَرِثُهٗ مَا يَقُوْلُ وَيَاْتِيْنَا فَرْدًا‏(80)\nWWANARESUH MAA YAQOOLO WAYAATEENAA FARDAN.\nAnd We will inherit what he spake of, and he shall come unto Us all alone.\nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اٰلِهَةً لِّيَكُوْنُوْا لَهُمْ عِزًّا ۙ‏(81)\nWAT-TAKHAZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE AALEHATAL LLEEKOONOOA LAHUM E’EZZAN.\nThey have taken gods besides God that they shall be unto them a source of strength,\nكَلَّا‌ ؕ سَيَكْفُرُوْنَ بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ وَيَكُوْنُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضِدًّا‏(82)\nKALLAA SA-YAKFOROON BEE’EBAADATEHEM WAYAKOONOONA A’LAYHIM ZEDDAN.\nBy no means! Soon shall they disavow their worship, and they shall unto them be adversaries.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ تَؤُزُّهُمْ اَزًّا ۙ‏(83)\nALAM TARA ANNAA ARSALNAA SHAYAATEENA A’LAL KAAFEREEN TAUZZUHUM AAZZAN.\nWhat! Seest thou not that We have sent satans against the dis believers to incite them with an incitement (to sin),\nفَلَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا نَعُدُّ لَهُمْ عَدًّا‌ ۚ‏(84)\nFALAA TAA’JAL A’LAYHIM INNAMAA NAU’UDDU LAHUM A’ADDAN.\nSo be not thou in haste against them, We only count unto them a limited number (of days).\nيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ اِلَى الرَّحْمٰنِ وَفْدًا‌ ۙ‏(85)\nYAWMA NAHSHORO MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN ELAL RAHMAANIR WAFDAN.\nOn the day (of resurrection) We will gather the pious ones unto the Beneficent (God) like the guests of honour,\nوَّنَسُوْقُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ وِرْدًا‌ ۘ‏(86)\nWWANASOOQU MUJREMEEN ELAA JAHANNAMA WERDAN.\nBut We will drive the guilty ones, unto Hell like (the thirsty) herd (to the watering place).\nلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ الشَّفَاعَةَ اِلَّا مَنِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمٰنِ عَهْدًا‌ ۘ‏(87)\nLAA YAMLEKOONA ASH-SHAFAAA’ATA ILLAA MANIS TAKHAZA I’NDAL RAHMAANIR A’HDAN.\nThey shall own not any intercession, save he who hath taken a promise from the Beneficent (God to do so).\nوَقَالُوْا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَلَدًا ؕ‏(88)\nWA QAALOO TAKHAZA RAHMAANO LAAHO.\nAnd say they: “The Beneficent (God) hath taken unto Him a son!\nلَقَدْ جِئْتُمْ شَيْئًا اِدًّا ۙ‏(89)\nLAQAD JETUM SHAY-ANW AEDDAN.\nIndeed, have ye put forth a thing (most) monstrous!\nتَكَادُ السَّمٰوٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرْنَ مِنْهُ وَتَنْشَقُّ الْاَرْضُ وَتَخِرُّ الْجِبَالُ هَدًّا ۙ‏(90)\nTAKAADO AS-SAMAAWAATU YATAFATTARNA MINHO WATANSHAQQU ARZO WATAKHERRU JEBAALO HADDAN.\nMight the heavens be almost rent thereat, and the earth cleaveth asunder, and the mountains fall down in fragments,\nاَنْ دَعَوْا لِلرَّحْمٰنِ وَلَدًا‌ ۚ‏(91)\nAN DA-A’W LELRRAHMAANE LAAHO.\nThat they should ascribe unto the Beneficent (God) a son!\nوَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا ؕ‏(92)\nWA MAA LAHAA LELRRAHMAANE AN YYATTAKHEZA LAAHO.\nAnd it behoveth not the Beneficent (God) that He should take (unto Him) (any one) a son.\nاِنْ كُلُّ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِلَّاۤ اٰتِى الرَّحْمٰنِ عَبْدًا ؕ‏(93)\nIN KULLO MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE ILLAA AAATEAA RAHMAANIR A’BDAN.\nNone there is in the heavens and the earth but must come unto the Beneficent (God) as a servant.\nلَقَدْ اَحْصٰٮهُمْ وَعَدَّهُمْ عَدًّا‏(94)\nLAQAD AAHSAAHUM WAA’ADDAHUM A’ADDAN.\nAnd indeed He hath an account of (all), and numbered them (with) an exact numbering.\nوَكُلُّهُمْ اٰتِيْهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَرْدًا‏(95)\nWAKULLUHUM AAATEEHE YAWMA QEYAAMATE FARDAN.\nAnd each one of them shall come unto him on the Day of Judgment, singly (alone).\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَيَجْعَلُ لَهُمُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وُدًّا‏(96)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SA-YAJ-A’LUL LAHOMUL RAHMAANO WUDDAN.\nVerily those who believe and work good deeds the Beneficent (God) will appoint love for them.\nفَاِنَّمَا يَسَّرْنٰهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لِتُبَشِّرَ بِهِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ وَتُنْذِرَ بِهٖ قَوْمًا لُّدًّا‏(97)\nFA-INNAMAA YASSARNAAHO BE-LESAANEKA LETUBASSHERA BEHIL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN WATUNZERA BEHI QAWMAN LLUDDAN.\nSo have We only made it (Qur’an) easy in thine own tongue that thou mayest give glad tidings thereby unto the pious ones, and warn by it a people (who are) contentious.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍؕ هَلْ تُحِسُّ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ اَوْ تَسْمَعُ لَهُمْ رِكْزًا‏(98)\nWA AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HAL TUHESSU MINHUM MIN AHADIM AW TASMAU’U LAHUM REKZAN.\nAnd how many of the generations We did destroy before them? Dost thou find out any one (anywhere)? or dost thou hear (even) a whisper (of them)?",
  "merits": "There are 99 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is written in the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan that the reward for reciting this Surah is equal to ten times the number of people present at the time of Prophets Zakariyyah (a.s.), Yahya (a.s.), Eesaa (a.s.), Moosa (a.s.), Ishaaq (a.s.), Haroon (a.s.), Ibrahim (a.s.), Ya’qoob (a.s.) and Ismaaeel (a.s.) combined.\nKeeping this Surah (written) in the house ensures protection from thieves and Allah (s.w.t.) blesses the occupants of the house. It is also narrated that before going in the presence of a tyrant ruler, if a person recites ‘Kaf-Ha-Ya-’Ain-Saad’ and closes, with each letter, one finger of his right hand, and then recites ‘Ha-Mim-‘Ain-Seen-Qaaf’ and with each letter, closes one finger of his left hand; and then he comes in the presence of the tyrant and recites ‘wa a’natil wojooho lil hayyil qayyoom wa khaaba man hamala zulma’ and then he opens his fingers, he will be protected from the evil of the tyrant."
